        "original_id": "fb52601b-e9db-5e1b-b4da-60dabdd466da",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Igor Borisovich Dmitriev, Rosencrantz, Guildenstern, Hamlet, King Claudius, Grigori Kozintsev, Yan Frid, Natalya Tenyakova, Vladimir Chestnokov\n- Products: Hamlet, The Green Carriage\n- Topics: Russian film and theater acting, Shakespearean characters, Soviet historical drama films\n\nFacts:\n- Igor Borisovich Dmitriev was born on May 29, 1927.\n- Rosencrantz and Guildenstern are childhood friends of Hamlet.\n- King Claudius summoned Rosencrantz and Guildenstern to distract Hamlet from his apparent madness and, if possible, discover its cause.\n- The Green Carriage is a 1967 Soviet historical drama film directed by Yan Frid.\n- The Green Carriage stars Natalya Tenyakova, Vladimir Chestnokov, and Igor Dmitriev.\n- Igor Borisovich Dmitriev was a Russian film and theater actor who specialized in aristocratic characters in costume productions.\n- Igor Borisovich Dmitriev played Rosencrantz in Grigori Kozintsev's Hamlet.\n- Igor Borisovich Dmitriev died on January 26, 2008.",
